{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00487",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.67,
      "end_seconds": 6.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Hi, you know, doctor, I brought my bag, is it fine to leave it here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.06,
      "end_seconds": 10.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.33,
      "end_seconds": 13.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.71,
      "end_seconds": 17.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.63,
      "end_seconds": 31.14,
      "duration_seconds": 12.51,
      "text": "Well, I've been having tightness in my chest when I walk. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.21,
      "end_seconds": 35.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.36,
      "end_seconds": 39.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Well, I've had it since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.98,
      "end_seconds": 42.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.14,
      "end_seconds": 46.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.63,
      "end_seconds": 51.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Have you had a heavy feeling in the left arm?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.76,
      "end_seconds": 67.41,
      "duration_seconds": 14.65,
      "text": "Yes, since last Tuesday. With heavy feeling in the left arm, a eight out of ten, I suppose. It settles a little with resting. Oh, and breathlessness on exertion. I've also had tiredness, for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.26,
      "end_seconds": 70.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Any palpitations or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.86,
      "end_seconds": 72.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.56,
      "end_seconds": 80.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any cough or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.9,
      "end_seconds": 84.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "No cough or fever, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.51,
      "end_seconds": 88.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Okay, anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.73,
      "end_seconds": 91.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.11,
      "end_seconds": 95.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "So, did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.6,
      "end_seconds": 99.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.4,
      "end_seconds": 101.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.71,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.55,
      "end_seconds": 107.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.65,
      "end_seconds": 109.59,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.6,
      "end_seconds": 112.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.3,
      "end_seconds": 117.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Right, what medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.05,
      "end_seconds": 121.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "It's metformin, 500 milligrams, maybe, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.22,
      "end_seconds": 126.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.89,
      "end_seconds": 134.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Hmm, not with me. I'll bring it next time. It's rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 135.95,
      "end_seconds": 144.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "I mean, um, doctor, I think the last prescription for the rosuvastatin was 20 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.89,
      "end_seconds": 149.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Alright, hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.86,
      "end_seconds": 154.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.7,
      "end_seconds": 159.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.22,
      "end_seconds": 171.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.38,
      "text": "I have diabetes. I have high cholesterol, for about ten years. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.97,
      "end_seconds": 173.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.45,
      "end_seconds": 177.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.47,
      "end_seconds": 192.31,
      "duration_seconds": 13.84,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.26,
      "end_seconds": 195.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.34,
      "end_seconds": 197.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.85,
      "end_seconds": 203.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.27,
      "end_seconds": 214.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.4,
      "end_seconds": 243.66,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.5 degrees, SpO2 98 percent on room air, heart rate 80, pressure 161 over 95."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.99,
      "end_seconds": 246.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.75,
      "end_seconds": 251.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment. Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.07,
      "end_seconds": 254.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Well, it's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.02,
      "end_seconds": 259.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.82,
      "end_seconds": 263.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.11,
      "end_seconds": 283.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, no murmurs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.31,
      "end_seconds": 285.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.52,
      "end_seconds": 288.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.57,
      "end_seconds": 300.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Lungs are clear and there's no swelling in your ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.02,
      "end_seconds": 323.41,
      "duration_seconds": 20.39,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Putting it all together, my working impression is angina-type chest pain. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep gastro-oesophageal reflux in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.47,
      "end_seconds": 334.55,
      "duration_seconds": 10.08,
      "text": "Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had tightness in your chest when you walk, since yesterday, moderate, and no palpitations or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.71,
      "end_seconds": 337.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.41,
      "end_seconds": 362.82,
      "duration_seconds": 24.41,
      "text": "Let's get a treadmill test, for exertional chest tightness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'd like to arrange an echocardiogram for chest tightness. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'm prescribing GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes, as needed. It's for chest tightness. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.6,
      "end_seconds": 366.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Okay, and I take that after food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.54,
      "end_seconds": 393.76,
      "duration_seconds": 26.22,
      "text": "Don't push through the chest tightness, stop, sit down, and use the spray if I've given it to you. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.3,
      "end_seconds": 397.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Okay, you know, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.11,
      "end_seconds": 408.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the chest tightness comes at rest or lasts more than fifteen minutes, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.23,
      "end_seconds": 410.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.99,
      "end_seconds": 420.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the results are back. I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.81,
      "end_seconds": 433.93,
      "duration_seconds": 11.12,
      "text": "So, um, I take the GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.33,
      "end_seconds": 440.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Right, yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.68,
      "end_seconds": 443.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "No questions. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}